          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Briscolone (large Briscola) with the full pack and Briscola-style point and trick scoring.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is determined by the turned card; follow suit when able. Point values (ace 11, three 10, king 4, queen 3, jack 2; others zero) are summed from captured tricks.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit; point values: ace 11, three 10, king 4, queen 3, jack 2, others zero. Trick order is standard; the first partnership to reach the target score (e.g. 121 or 61) wins the game.',
